      "url": "https://www.google.com/maps/@13.6327770,123.2689804,80m/data=!3m1!1e3",
      "note": "Inspected owner-supplied san-isidro-schools.png on 2026-10-08; capture date unknown. URL locates the site. Hand re-traced on 2026-10-08 from the owner image at enlarged scale: every distinguishable crown, canopy belt, lawn, planted bed, garden plot, hedge, path, apron, court and parking area is traced where the image shows it, and bare ground stays bare. Shares one owner image with San Isidro National High. Forest canopy fills the north of the campus around the pale-roofed block; canopy fills the strip south of the high school and the east group between the east blocks; crowns stand between the classroom roofs and along the frontage. The tan walkway between the dark and light classroom roofs and the packed front apron along the road are hardscape; the low green patches beside the high school boundary and south of the high school are grass, and the striped vegetable-garden plot north of the classroom blocks is planting. Registration: continuous triangulated image registration; independent check errors 2.14 m, 1.17 m, 8.29 m, 8.23 m. Trunks sit inside their observed crowns; crowns may overhang roofs and roads. Complete mapped roofs, pitches, full-width paths/roads, water and farmland remain unchanged. Ground under opaque canopy is not invented. No surveyed boundary, species, construction date or exact inventory inferred; no bitmap ships."
